Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Cicadas Boil the Highline Cable
- Story & Context: When harbor-police skiffs encircled the dripping scaffolding of Oshima Spire during the torrential squall of August 2091, sound-runner Jax "Needle" Vane refused to cut the generator lines. As five hundred kids in grease-soaked diving suits stamped their creepers into three inches of tidal run-off, Mona shoved her piccolo into a blown megaphone to counter the police acoustic-cannons with a deafening 140-BPM counter-frequency. As the transformer hissed blue fire into the wet air, Jax grabbed the battered chrome mic and screamed, "Shake your thorax till the ballast breaks!" igniting a dancing riot that swamped two patrol boats.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: High-contrast retro-cyberpunk album art showing a swarm of metallic cicadas chewing through sparking high-voltage electrical cables above a flooded cityscape, glowing green sparks falling into dark ocean foam, retro-futuristic greaser typography.

Track 2: "Why Strip the Chrysalis Now?"
- Story & Context: Sheltered in the rusted ventilation flues of Battery Wharf while coast guard searchlights swept the brackish water, Mona confessed to Deacon that she had bartered their last spare vacuum tube to pay off a local syndicate for clean oxygen tanks. The bitter argument dissolved into an impromptu, sweat-drenched jam in the cramped sheet-metal tunnel, Deacon slapping his upright bass against the aluminum walls to mimic the thudding drone propellers overhead. With tears cutting clean tracks through the carbon grime on her cheeks, Mona looked Deacon in the eyes and belted out, "Why strip the chrysalis now, when the wings ain't dry and the salt's on your mouth?" as her piccolo shrieked through a chorus pedal.
