Track 3: Sister Chitin of Rooftop Zero
- Story & Context: By sunrise after the great raid, Rooftop Zero was completely submerged beneath the swell, leaving only a radio transmitter antennae wrapped in translucent, molted hulls of saltwater locusts. Urban folklore across the pontoon slums says Deacon stayed behind on the sinking deck with his piezo-rigged bass to broadcast an infrasonic wobble that jammed the sonar of corporate salvage vessels. Watermen still claim that when the gale winds hit the antennae at low tide, you can hear his yodel echoing across the flotsam alongside the lyric: "When the tide takes the spire, we'll teach the flukes to sting."
